WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:07.020
"The Best Mouthwash for
Halitosis (Bad Breath)"

00:00:07.020 --> 00:00:10.380
Bad breath is an
underestimated problem affecting

00:00:10.380 --> 00:00:12.600
a significant proportion
of the global population.

00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:15.600
It seems most people
regularly report

00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:17.580
encountering people
with halitosis.

00:00:17.580 --> 00:00:21.360
Masking agents are frequently
used to cover up bad breath,

00:00:21.360 --> 00:00:22.620
but studies have shown
that the use

00:00:22.620 --> 00:00:25.140
of mouth rinses, sprays,
or mints containing

00:00:25.140 --> 00:00:26.640
an agreeable masking odor

00:00:26.640 --> 00:00:27.900
only have a short-term effect,

00:00:27.900 --> 00:00:30.120
since you're not treating
the underlying cause,

00:00:30.120 --> 00:00:33.000
so the exclusive usage
of masking products

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:34.800
can never be truly considered

00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:37.080
an effective solution
to the problem.

00:00:38.160 --> 00:00:41.820
The cause of bad breath
is oral putrefaction,

00:00:41.820 --> 00:00:44.040
the degradation
of certain amino acids

00:00:44.040 --> 00:00:45.960
mostly derived
by bacterial breakdown

00:00:45.960 --> 00:00:47.280
of proteins in your mouth.

00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:49.500
Specifically,
bacteria degrade

00:00:49.500 --> 00:00:51.240
the sulfur-containing
amino acids,

00:00:51.240 --> 00:00:52.915
such as cysteine
and methionine,

00:00:52.915 --> 00:00:53.940
into stinky compounds

00:00:53.940 --> 00:00:56.160
like the rotten egg gas
hydrogen sulfide,

00:00:56.160 --> 00:00:58.560
so-called
volatile sulfur compounds.

00:00:59.160 --> 00:01:02.340
If you measure these compounds
spewing out of people's mouths

00:01:02.340 --> 00:01:04.620
with machines
with names like Breathtron,

00:01:04.620 --> 00:01:07.800
tooth brushing alone
does not significantly reduce

00:01:07.800 --> 00:01:09.660
oral malodor.

00:01:09.660 --> 00:01:12.480
Brushing alone reduces
sulfur breath compounds

00:01:12.480 --> 00:01:15.000
from more than 450
down to about 300,

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:18.840
but that's still above the
stinky breath threshold of 250.

00:01:18.840 --> 00:01:21.120
Add tongue cleaning

00:01:21.120 --> 00:01:23.820
and you can drop that down
to right around the threshold,

00:01:23.820 --> 00:01:25.980
but adding
an antiseptic mouthwash--

00:01:25.980 --> 00:01:28.800
an antibacterial mouthwash--
did even better.

00:01:28.800 --> 00:01:32.220
Okay, so what's
the best mouthwash to use?

00:01:32.880 --> 00:01:36.540
To find out, researchers used
the cysteine challenge test.

00:01:36.540 --> 00:01:38.700
Instead of giving people
dairy products,

00:01:38.700 --> 00:01:40.200
which contain
the protein casein,

00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:42.540
which is rich in the sulfur
amino acid cysteine,

00:01:42.540 --> 00:01:44.040
they just had the participants

00:01:44.040 --> 00:01:45.960
swish directly
with some cysteine

00:01:45.960 --> 00:01:49.200
and then followed effectiveness
using odor-ograms.

00:01:49.200 --> 00:01:51.420
For example, toothbrushing.

00:01:51.420 --> 00:01:53.640
When people
swished with cysteine

00:01:53.640 --> 00:01:54.600
before brushing their teeth,

00:01:54.600 --> 00:01:57.000
here's the spike
in stinky sulfur compounds

00:01:57.000 --> 00:01:58.560
spewing out of their mouths.

00:01:58.560 --> 00:02:00.480
When they brushed their teeth
with water

00:02:00.480 --> 00:02:03.540
and swished again at various
times over the rest of the day,

00:02:03.540 --> 00:02:05.340
the spikes pretty much
looked the same,

00:02:05.340 --> 00:02:07.980
meaning toothbrushing with water
didn't remove

00:02:07.980 --> 00:02:09.420
many bad breath bacteria,

00:02:09.420 --> 00:02:11.700
since the subjects were
spewing out similar spikes

00:02:11.700 --> 00:02:13.080
starting just 20 minutes later.

00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:16.440
Brushing with toothpaste
works better.

00:02:16.440 --> 00:02:19.380
See how it knocks down the
next spike of stinky compounds

00:02:19.380 --> 00:02:22.500
before the bacteria slowly
grow back throughout the day?

00:02:23.460 --> 00:02:25.380
What about using
a tongue scraper?

00:02:25.380 --> 00:02:26.760
Here's the odor-ogram.

00:02:26.760 --> 00:02:29.940
Tongue scraping knocks it down
by about half

00:02:29.940 --> 00:02:32.220
before coming back
over the next few hours.

00:02:32.880 --> 00:02:34.440
What about chewing gum?

00:02:34.440 --> 00:02:36.360
Here's that odor-ogram.

00:02:37.440 --> 00:02:40.980
Some effect that disappears
over the subsequent few hours.

00:02:41.940 --> 00:02:43.920
What about various mouthwashes?

00:02:43.920 --> 00:02:46.320
First of all,
rinsing with water.

00:02:46.920 --> 00:02:47.760
Useless.

00:02:48.720 --> 00:02:50.400
Can be helpful
for morning breath,

00:02:50.400 --> 00:02:52.680
to rinse any stagnation
that occurred overnight,

00:02:52.680 --> 00:02:54.660
but during the day,
just rinsing with water

00:02:54.660 --> 00:02:57.060
isn't clearing
many bad breath bacteria.

00:02:57.060 --> 00:03:00.300
And swishing
with Scope mouthwash?

00:03:00.300 --> 00:03:03.060
Just as useless as water.

00:03:03.960 --> 00:03:06.060
Scope is
an anti-bacterial mouthwash

00:03:06.060 --> 00:03:07.920
but it must not be good
at killing

00:03:07.920 --> 00:03:10.200
the specific bacteria
that cause bad breath.

00:03:10.200 --> 00:03:12.420
Peridex, though, cleaned house,

00:03:12.420 --> 00:03:15.060
killing off those bacteria
even seven hours later.

00:03:15.060 --> 00:03:17.100
What is Peridex?

00:03:17.100 --> 00:03:19.440
That's just a brand name
for chlorhexidine.

00:03:20.340 --> 00:03:25.020
Uh-oh: We know about that
from this video.

00:03:25.020 --> 00:03:28.440
Chlorhexidine doesn't just get
rid of bad breath bacteria;

00:03:28.440 --> 00:03:30.840
it also kills off
the good bacteria on your tongue

00:03:30.840 --> 00:03:32.520
that help you make nitric oxide,

00:03:32.520 --> 00:03:33.660
which protects your arteries,

00:03:33.660 --> 00:03:36.240
and so chlorhexidine can raise
your blood pressure.

00:03:36.240 --> 00:03:38.040
And that's not all.

00:03:38.040 --> 00:03:40.140
Chlorhexidine
can stain your teeth.

00:03:40.140 --> 00:03:43.560
That's not what you want
in a mouthwash.

00:03:43.560 --> 00:03:46.680
Adverse effects are not rare.

00:03:46.680 --> 00:03:50.400
Tooth staining, the buildup
of tartar, taste disturbance,

00:03:50.400 --> 00:03:53.040
and damage to the lining of the
mouth have all been reported

00:03:53.040 --> 00:03:55.980
with the use of chlorhexidine
in about 9 out of 10 people.

00:03:55.980 --> 00:03:58.860
88 percent of people suffer
various side effects.

00:03:58.860 --> 00:04:00.960
But hey, chlorhexidine
may be better

00:04:00.960 --> 00:04:03.480
than mouthwashes
with hydrogen peroxide,

00:04:03.480 --> 00:04:05.820
which may be carcinogenic,

00:04:05.820 --> 00:04:07.800
potentially increasing
your risk of mouth cancer.

00:04:07.800 --> 00:04:11.280
That's not just based
on studies on rodents, either.

00:04:11.280 --> 00:04:13.740
Cultures of human
mouth lining cells

00:04:13.740 --> 00:04:15.660
show significant DNA damage.

00:04:16.200 --> 00:04:19.680
Triclosan was another
common antibacterial ingredient

00:04:19.680 --> 00:04:20.580
in mouthwashes,

00:04:20.580 --> 00:04:23.700
now effectively banned
in over-the-counter products.

00:04:24.420 --> 00:04:27.120
Tongue scraping alone
doesn't always resolve

00:04:27.120 --> 00:04:28.440
the problem of halitosis.

00:04:28.440 --> 00:04:30.000
So, what can we use?

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:31.920
If bad breath persists

00:04:31.920 --> 00:04:33.900
after improving tongue
and dental hygiene,

00:04:33.900 --> 00:04:37.380
an active zinc-based mouth rinse
can be introduced.

00:04:37.380 --> 00:04:40.920
Zinc binds directly to
the volatile sulfur compounds

00:04:40.920 --> 00:04:42.900
and prevents them from
gassing out of your mouth.

00:04:42.900 --> 00:04:46.500
Mouth rinses containing
ZnCl without alcohol

00:04:46.500 --> 00:04:49.140
have been found to instantly
though temporarily

00:04:49.140 --> 00:04:51.480
be effective for halitosis.

00:04:51.480 --> 00:04:54.480
Researchers looked
at eight mouth rinses,

00:04:54.480 --> 00:04:57.180
and the most effective
was a zinc chloride one

00:04:57.180 --> 00:04:59.940
and the least effective
was Colgate Plax.

00:04:59.940 --> 00:05:02.700
In fact, both of the alcohol
rinses were found to be

00:05:02.700 --> 00:05:03.780
the least effective.

00:05:03.780 --> 00:05:06.720
The thought is that they
may exacerbate halitosis

00:05:06.720 --> 00:05:07.800
by drying up your mouth.

00:05:08.400 --> 00:05:10.980
Here are some cysteine challenge
testing results

00:05:10.980 --> 00:05:13.080
with different concentrations
of zinc chloride.

00:05:13.080 --> 00:05:16.860
Note that all forms of zinc
don't work the same though.

00:05:16.860 --> 00:05:18.660
Zinc chloride is very effective,

00:05:18.660 --> 00:05:21.060
but zinc gluconate, which was
the difference between

00:05:21.060 --> 00:05:24.420
regular Listerine
and an "advanced" Listerine,

00:05:24.420 --> 00:05:26.220
didn't seem to work as well.

